Remove the now-obsolete bulk state-transfer machinery and close remaining backend-to-TUI bypasses. Delete TuiRuntimeStateSnapshot, TuiSubmitResult::state_snapshot, snapshot-bearing keybinding/reload results, the app state_snapshot builder and the apply_runtime_state_snapshot helper chain once their state and transition responsibilities have migrated. Reduce TuiRuntimeOptions to genuinely immutable frontend startup dependencies and neutral action/interaction endpoints, or replace it with an appropriately narrow frontend entry contract; it must no longer contain a duplicate initial copy of every canonical state domain.

Audit all TUI includes and runtime callback signatures for Session/session_ts, stores, coordinator types, backend permission internals and other implementation dependencies. Keep backend bindings under app/frontend or app/tui and give TUI only the neutral frontend API. Move existing ModelSelection/SessionStats registration details behind that boundary if necessary without changing their canonical ownership or dirty/refresh behavior. Do not introduce module cycles, weaken dependency guards or leak paths/capabilities through opaque-looking containers.

All observable backend state reaches TuiFrontEnd projection members through UnlockedData notifications and foo_refresh accessors. Command results may report success, errors and necessary control outcomes, but cannot carry arbitrary replacement presentation state. UI-local ComposerSnapshot, draft undo snapshots and private projection snapshots can remain only when constructed and used locally; document this distinction and verify their producers. Remove obsolete tests/helpers rather than retaining dead compatibility shims, replacing their assertions with equivalent new-boundary behavior tests. A whole-tree source/signature audit must find no transported Snapshot contracts or differently named state bypasses.
